[quote=]Does anyone see how to get any lower bounds for the maximum possible number of edges in a rectangle $k$-visibility graph with $n$ vertices?

Also, what are upper and lower bounds for the maximum possible number of edges in a $d$-dimensional rectangle $k$-visibility graph with $n$ vertices?[/quote]

One obvious lower bound for $n>k$ is $n(k+1)-\frac{(k+1)(k+2)}2,$ which comes from putting $d$-dimensional cubes in a row, like so:

[hide=Diagram][asy]import three;
currentprojection=perspective(1/5,4/3,1/6);
for (int i=0; i<5; ++i) {
draw(shift((0,2*i,0))*unitcube,rgb(0.6,1,0.7));
}
[/asy]
[/hide]

