Excellent work. You showed that the complete graph on $2d$ vertices can be represented as a $d$-dimensional rectangle visibility graph. If we modify your construction slightly, can we show that the complete graph on $2d+1$ vertices can be represented as a $d$-dimensional rectangle visibility graph?

If we extend your construction to $d$-dimensional rectangle $k$-visibility graphs, what bound do we get on the maximum $n$ such that the complete graph on $n$ vertices can be represented as a $d$-dimensional rectangle $k$-visibility graph?

