After the cop picks an initial vertex, the killer picks a vertex of the same color of distance 2 away from the cop. 

On each succeeding turn, the killer moves towards the cop onto a vertex of the same color as the cop's. The cop will eventually be cornered.
[/indent]
[/list]
So, killer-win graphs exist if and only if $k \ge 3.$

